{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>YHWH…</b> For we too have served You. As for <b>ba'alu־nu</b> (they lorded it over us): it means they were our masters, like <b>yashiv</b> (shall restore) to its owner <small>(Exodus 21:34)</small>. And yet we would mention Your name. And the sense of <b>levad'kha</b> (You alone) is that You helped us, as if to say: there is no help but in You; therefore it is for us to mention You."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:19.123296858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}